gap: 3-10
scene: The best pupil {N} has ever taught, seventeen and gifted, has won a place at the music college. Now they want to turn it down and go on the road with a band, and their parents ask {N} to talk them out of it.
scene W: {N} owes the pupil the truth and the parents respect. It is not {Ns} life to choose.
scene U: Seven years of scales and theory have made this pupil ready for the college. The road could waste all of it in a year.
scene B: A pupil at the music college is the best name a teacher can have. Parents all over town would hear of it.
scene R: {N} remembers wanting exactly this at seventeen, saying no, and wondering ever since.
scene G: The pupil's grandmother first brought them to {Ns} door at ten. The whole family has gathered behind the college place.
- W | tell the parents it is the pupil's choice, and stay out of it | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: arts.W | chance: 75
- U | ask the college whether the place could be held for a year | v: achievement, security | sphere: arts.U | chance: 75
- B | talk the pupil round: the college first, the band after, with the better name | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.B | chance: 75
- R | tell the pupil to go on the road while they are young enough to love it | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: arts.R | chance: 75
- G | sit down with the whole family, the grandmother too, and talk it through | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: arts.G | chance: 75
- W>G | promise the family to keep teaching the pupil, whichever way they go | v: benevolence | sphere: arts.W | chance: 65
- U>W | set out both roads on paper for the pupil: the money, the years, the odds | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: arts.U | chance: 65
- B>U | ring an old friend at the college to have the place quietly put back a year | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.B | chance: 65
- R>B | go and hear the band, then tell the pupil straight whether it is good enough | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: arts.R | chance: 65
- G>R | play the pupil's first-ever piece together, and let them decide after | v: tradition, hedonism | sphere: arts.G | chance: 65
works: The pupil chooses with a clear head, and sends {N} a postcard from wherever the choice leads.
works: The parents thank {N} for the talk, and the family stay close to {N} for years.
fails: The pupil makes the choice in a temper, and the family blame {N} for it.
fails: The pupil stops coming to lessons, and {N} hears the news second-hand from {friend}.

