- R | preach next week on giving freely, with nothing asked back | v: self-direction | sphere: faith.R | chance: 75
- G | visit the giver's family at home and talk it over at their table | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: faith.G | chance: 75
- W>R | refuse the request, and tell the hall plainly why from the front | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | sphere: faith.W | chance: 65
- U>G | ask the oldest members how the halls they knew before handled this | v: tradition | sphere: faith.U | chance: 65
- B>W | write the hall's rules down: no gift buys a seat or a sermon | v: conformity, power | sphere: faith.B | chance: 65
- R>U | go looking for a cheaper room that same week, ready to move | v: self-direction, security | sphere: faith.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask the founding families to give a little more each, so no one giver holds sway | v: tradition, security | sphere: faith.G | chance: 65
works: The hall pays its rent through the winter, and the sermons stay {Ns} own.
works: The giver stays, and in time becomes one of the hall's steadiest members.
fails: The giver leaves with their family, and the rent is due in six weeks.
fails: The hall splits into two camps over it, and {friend} says half the chairs are empty now.

