earth: a regular client who comes for her back mentions a new numbness down one leg, and says she would rather keep seeing you than go to her doctor
times: Most complementary therapists, a few times; clients sometimes bring a new symptom to a therapist first, and the training says to send them on to a doctor (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A regular client of {Ns}, who comes for her back, mentions a new numbness down one leg. She says she trusts {N} more than her doctor, and would rather just book more sessions.
scene W: {Ns} course was clear about this: a new numbness goes to a doctor, whatever the client would prefer.
scene U: {N} knows what the sessions can do for a stiff back, and that numbness is something else. It needs a proper look.
scene B: She is {Ns} best client, three sessions a month, and she has said she will go elsewhere if anyone pushes her.
scene R: {N} feels a jolt of alarm, and wants to act today, not after another session.
scene G: Her daughter lives two streets away. {N} has known the family since the practice opened.
- W | stop the session and tell her this needs a doctor this week | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | ask careful questions and write down what she describes, to take to her doctor | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | tell her the next booking waits until she has seen a doctor | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | ring her surgery with her, there and then, and book the appointment | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | ask whether her daughter could go with her to the doctor | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>U | give her a written note for the doctor, with the date the numbness began | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>B | explain plainly what the sessions can and cannot do, and keep her trust | v: universalism, security | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>R | offer a free session once she has been to the doctor, as a nudge | v: benevolence, hedonism | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>G | walk her down to the surgery after the session, and wait with her | v: benevolence | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>W | ring her daughter, with her say-so, so the family see that she goes | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: She sees her doctor that week, and comes back to {N} for her back once the doctor says it is fine.
works: She thanks {N} for being straight with her, and sends a friend to the practice.
fails: She cancels her next sessions, and {N} never learns whether she went.
fails: She is cross at being pushed, and {colleague} hears she has booked with someone across town.

