scene: A new practice opens down the road, run by {rival}, with posters saying its treatments cure illness. Two of {Ns} clients ask why {N} never promises the same, and one has already booked there.
scene W: The advertising rules say no one may claim to cure an illness without proof. {N} has always kept to them.
scene U: {N} has read what the studies show: the sessions ease tension and help people feel cared for, and that is all they show.
scene B: Bold promises fill appointment books, and {Ns} own book has three empty mornings this week.
scene R: The posters make {N} angry. People who are really ill could skip the doctor because of them.
scene G: Most of {Ns} clients have come for years and send their friends. That trust was built slowly, one honest word at a time.
- W | report the cure claims to the body that checks advertising | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | put a plain card at the desk: what the sessions can and cannot do | v: universalism | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | compete on comfort and price, and promise nothing you cannot keep | act: compete on comfort and price, and promise nothing they cannot keep | v: achievement, security | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | go down the road and tell the rival to their face the posters are wrong | v: self-direction, universalism | mark: made an enemy | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | trust the old clients' word of mouth, and change nothing | v: tradition, security | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>B | join the therapists' register that bans cure claims, and show its badge | v: conformity, security | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>R | give a free evening talk at the library on how to judge health claims | v: universalism, stimulation | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>G | build friendly ties with the local surgery, so clients who need more go there | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>W | tell every client who asks, straight out, that nothing here cures illness | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the older therapists in town how they kept clients through such fads | v: tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: Clients drift back within the year, and several say they trust {N} more for the plain words.
works: The cure posters come down after a complaint, and {Ns} book fills again.
fails: The month is thin, and two more regulars try the practice down the road.
fails: {rival} spreads word that {N} is jealous, and the row goes round the town.
